From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] topology: reconcile clients from topology responses

EasyMesh Topology Notifications are multicast and unacknowledged. The agent
used them as the only source of client placement, even though the standard
Associated Clients TLV is explicitly allowed in a Topology Response. A lost
notification therefore left the controller's STA parent stale indefinitely.

Emit the Associated Clients TLV from the agent's consolidated STA model and
consume it on every controller Topology Response, not only during initial
topology synchronization. Reported associations are inserted through the
normal pending STA update path; its single-association enforcement removes a
previous BSS attribution and preserves an existing capability frame.

Poll synchronized agents every 15 seconds. The notification remains the
low-latency path while this standard query/response exchange is the bounded
repair path. The optional TLV is bounded by both one standard message buffer
and the exact capacity left in the two-buffer response after all mandatory
and implementation-specific TLVs have been generated.

